flowchart TB

  v_complete["The pipeline handler must <br/>call completeRequest from <br/>the CameraManager thread to <br/>signal completion. It may <br/>pass completed requests in <br/>any order, and the function <br/>returns them to the <br/>application in submission <br/>order. The request must not <br/>be accessed after the <br/>function returns."]
  v_dispatch["doQueueRequests ends when <br/>the waiting list is empty. <br/>Even when the list is not <br/>empty, it stops the loop if <br/>the size of queuedRequests#95; <br/>equals <br/>maxQueuedRequestsDevice#95; or <br/>the front request is not <br/>prepared."]
  v_queue["On the normal path, the <br/>request is removed from the <br/>waiting list before it is <br/>passed to doQueueRequest. <br/>On the stop path, after <br/>stopDevice returns, a <br/>detached request is marked <br/>cancelled and passed to it."]
  v_stop["stop is called from the <br/>CameraManager thread. Its <br/>contract requires it to <br/>stop capture and request <br/>processing immediately, <br/>cancel unfinished requests, <br/>and complete them <br/>immediately in an error <br/>state."]
  v_stopdevice["The stopDevice implementer <br/>must immediately stop <br/>capture on all running <br/>streams and request <br/>processing, cancel already <br/>submitted unfinished <br/>requests, and complete them <br/>immediately in an error <br/>state. stop handles the <br/>detached waiting requests <br/>after stopDevice returns."]
  v_complete -->|"After handling completions, <br/>completeRequest calls <br/>doQueueRequests to allow <br/>waiting requests to proceed."| v_dispatch
  v_dispatch -->|"If the waiting list is not <br/>empty, the size of <br/>queuedRequests#95; differs <br/>from <br/>maxQueuedRequestsDevice#95;, <br/>and the front request is <br/>prepared, doQueueRequests <br/>removes the request before <br/>calling doQueueRequest in <br/>case of a recursive call. · <br/>#33;request-#62;#95;d#40;#41;-#62;prepared#95; <br/>#91;false#93;"| v_queue
  v_stop -->|"stop separates <br/>waitingRequests#95; into <br/>waitingRequests, then calls <br/>stopDevice. This separation <br/>prevents waiting requests <br/>from being requeued in <br/>response to a <br/>completeRequest call inside <br/>stopDevice."| v_stopdevice
  v_stop -->|"After stopDevice returns, <br/>stop removes each detached <br/>request, marks it <br/>cancelled, and calls <br/>doQueueRequest to preserve <br/>order. This gives each <br/>request a sequence number <br/>and temporarily adds it to <br/>queuedRequests#95; so <br/>completeRequest can <br/>complete it properly."| v_queue
